@4.17 COMBO.INC.BL -- a drop-down list that folds into one row
.
=4.17 COMBO.INC.BL -- A DROP-DOWN LIST THAT FOLDS INTO ONE ROW
.
=DESCRIPTION
.
.  COMBO.ADD
.      IN: COMBO.X% COMBO.Y% COMBO.W% COMBO.SEL%
.      OUT: COMBO.CTRL%
.
:GP.SUB FORM.BEGIN, "TITLE", "MSG", "", 6, 40, "&OK", "&CANCEL"
:GP.SUB FORM.ITEMS, MY.BANK%, MY.ADDR
:STATE = GP.FN(FORM.COMBO, 1, "STATE", 6, 12, 1)
:GP.SUB FORM.ITEM, "TEXAS"
:GP.SUB FORM.ITEM, "OHIO"
:IF GP.FN(FORMTO.RUN) THEN <OK>
:SEL = GP.FN(FORM.SEL, STATE)
:GP.SUB FORM.END
.
.A program reaches a combo through the FORM. verbs of GUI-DIALOGS.INC.BL (SEC
.4.12). GUI.FORM dispatches a GUI.CT.COMBO control to COMBO.DRAW, COMBO.KEY
.and COMBO.OPEN by name.
.
.COMBO.X% and COMBO.Y% are the closed control's top left, in cells. COMBO.W%
.is the width, brackets included. 5 is the floor and anything less is raised
.to it. COMBO.SEL% is the item showing, 1 up. COMBO.CTRL% is the control's
.number, 0 if the form was full.
.
.The items are the form's item store: GUI.ITEM.CLAIM after COMBO.ADD, then a
.GUI.ITEM.ADD each. GUI.ITEM.SEAL draws the combo once they are in. The
.choice is GUI.CTRL.SEL%(COMBO.CTRL%).
.
.The dropdown saves the cells it covers where the dialog does, by
.GUI.SAVEMODE% (SEC 4.11). In VRAM mode it takes a STASHVRAM handle of its
.own and needs no bank. In bank mode it goes in the dialog's save space, bank
.GUI.BANK% from GUI.STASHADDR, above the dialog's own save. Every combo on
.the form opens into that one slot, one at a time. If there is no room either
.way, the dropdown does not open.
.
.The dropdown is the popup slot of MENU.INC.BL (SEC 4.6), loaded from the
.item store each time it opens, so whatever the caller last built in that
.slot is gone after. An item is a menu row: & marks a hot key and "-" is a
.separator. The MENU.* colours and flags it sets are put back.
.
.A long list belongs in a list control. The dropdown shows every item at
.once, 32 at most, and does not scroll.
.
.The dropdown is framed like the dialog behind it. With GUI.GLYPH% non-zero
.it draws from GUI.EDGE.H%, GUI.EDGE.V%, GUI.CORNER.TL%, .TR, .BL and .BR,
.the same six a dialog frames with, so a re-ordered charset gets its own
.frame here too. With GUI.GLYPH% = 0 the frame is GP.BOX style 1.
.
.It is required by GUI.INC.BL, which names COMBO.DRAW and COMBO.KEY. BASLOAD
.resolves every label in a file, so a program that includes the GUI and
.leaves this one out stops with LABEL NOT FOUND whether it ever draws a combo
.or not. It needs MENU.INC.BL, and what that requires.
.
=SEE ALSO
.
>90|4.12 GUI-DIALOGS.INC.BL -- every dialog as a verb
>88|4.11 GUI.INC.BL -- the box that puts the screen back, and the form in 
>79|4.6 MENU.INC.BL -- menus built a row at a time
>96|4.17 COMBO.INC.BL -- a drop-down list that folds into one row
